  "headline": "Noise-aware PFN reading the noisy tables (n 32-8192, 20 cells): calibrated everywhere (over-confidence -0.010 to +0.019) and better in NLL than the release's own classifier in 20/20 cells (plain release) and 14/20 (tree release). At n*eps >= 32,768 it removes plain margins' structural over-confidence (-0.008..+0.005 vs +0.076..+0.087 for the naive-Bayes plug-in). The noise-aware analyst prefers the tree release in every cell from n*eps = 8192.0; at n <= 128 the table reader is within -0.036..-0.001 (plain) and -0.053..-0.000 (tree) nats of the row-reading noise-aware PFNs."
